              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Debilyn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was very good. I used a bag of frozen cut broccoli and splenda.",
            "datePublished": "2003-09-24T08:40:46.483Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "kath51"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The salad is served with raw brocolli, as one reader asked. I have made the recipe with the following. 2 bunches broccoli, 8 slices of fried bacon, 3/4 cup cheddar or swiss cheese - grated, 1 thinly slice red or white onion. Toss together. For the dressing: 1 cup mayo (no miracle whip) 1/2 cup sugar, 2 tablespoons white vinegar. Pour over broccoli mixture before eating or ahead of time, the longer it sets, the better tasting.(I have doubled the dressing mixture, we like a saucy texture to this salad. This broccoli salad has been around for a while, but once you make it, you always come back for the recipe. (bacon bits can be substituted for the bacon, although better tasting with fried bacon).",
            "datePublished": "2011-06-04T09:41:21.940Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Catlin"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Super easy salad! I used a package of real bacon bits instead of frying up some bacon. Left all the other measurements the same. Loved the dressing this made, I didn't find anything to overpower another. I did, however, mix this up in the evening and let it sit over night. I think that probably helped the flavors to really come together.",
            "datePublished": "2010-11-28T09:46:48.893Z"
          },
